{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "Reminders (docs/reminders.md). 'due': the local date and time a reminder fires, from the reminder ('fireAt', or 'offsetMinutes' before the task's planned time, plus its state and 'snoozedUntil') and its task; null means it never fires. 'quietHours': what the window [start, end) does to a reminder due at 'at'; a window whose start equals its end is off, and important reminders pass. 'snooze': where each snooze option lands, counted from 'now' with the day starting at 'dayStartHour'; 'tomorrowMorning' is 'morningHour' on the day after the current planning day. 'schedule': what a device does when it looks: 'due' lists the reminders that arrive after 'since' (the last look) up to and including 'now', soonest first; 'next' is the first one after 'now', the one the alarm is armed for. Reminders and tasks in 'schedule' and 'stale' leave out fields that keep their defaults (no offset, pending, not snoozed, not important; a task open with no day or time). 'stale': which of the notifications on screen ('shown', reminder ids) have to go at 'now' because their reminder was handled, snoozed, moved or deleted, or its task finished; sorted by id. 'ritual': the evening Plan tomorrow reminder at 'time' (null: off). For a planning day D it rings at the first moment of D whose clock reads 'time' (after midnight when 'time' is before the day's start), unless D is in 'ran' (done or skipped on any device); quiet hours don't move it. 'due' is today's planning day when its moment came after 'since' and up to 'now', never an earlier day; 'next' is the moment the alarm waits for. 'ritualStale': whether a reminder on screen for 'day' has to go, because it ran or the planning day moved on. 'ritualIds': a run's id is a UUID version 5 of '<owner, lower case>/<ritual>/<day>' in 'runNamespace'. 'reviewReminders': the review reminders (docs/reviews.md): a weekly one rings on the owner's 'weekday' (1 Monday to 7 Sunday), a monthly one on the first day of a month, at 'time' on the planning day, once per day, and never on a day already in 'ran'; 'due' is the planning day to show now and 'next' the moment the alarm waits for, as in 'ritual'. 'reviewPeriods': the period a reminder on 'day' looks back on: the week that is ending when it falls on a Saturday or Sunday, the week just gone earlier in the week, and the month just gone for a monthly reminder.",
  "morningHour": 8,
